["EmoRAG : Evaluating RAG Robustness to Symbolic Perturbations DOI: XXXXXXX.XXXXXXX Conference: 32nd ACM SIGKDD Conference on Knowledge Discovery and Data Mining; August 9-13, 2026; Jeju, Korea ISBN: 978-1-4503-XXXX-X/2018/06
2. Background and Related Work
2.1. RAG systems
The RAG system operates in two stages: retrieval and generation . In the retrieval stage, given a query q q , the retriever R R searches the knowledge database 𝒦 \mathcal{K} and ranks documents based on relevance: D = R ⁡ ( q , 𝒦 ) D=R(q,\mathcal{K}) , where D D is the set of top-ranked documents. Embedding-based methods like dense passage retrieval (
[Karpukhin et al. 2020](#bib.bib35)
) ensure query-document alignment in a shared vector space. In the generation stage, the retrieved documents D D are combined with the query q q by the generator G G , typically a pre-trained language model, to produce the final response: r ^ = G ⁡ ( q , D ) \hat{r}=G(q,D) , in which D D serves as additional text. The generator ensures responses are linguistically fluent and contextually accurate.
